For each risk, the manufacturer shall determine one or more of the risk treatment options and solutions so
that no unreasonable risks remain.
Risk treatment options:
— Mitigate risk – implement security controls (e.g. access control, secure coding, minimization of data,
  resiliency against denial of service attacks and secure communication protocols);
— Share risk (e.g. insurance, supplier sharing);
— Avoid risk (e.g. eliminate function);
— Accept risk – retain the risk.
The manufacturer shall create a risk report [WP-5.8-01] including the following:
— If risk mitigation, then define and document the goals for the controls that are identified to mitigate the risk;
— If risk sharing, then define and document the strategy and rationale for how the risks are shared with others;
— If risk avoidance, then define and document the strategy for how the risks are avoided;
— If risk acceptance, define and document the rationale for accepting and retaining the risk.
NOTE      It is expected that risks with risk ratings less than a certain threshold will be accepted. The manufacturer
can determine this risk threshold.

